course: dictionary
lesson: 7625
title: A long word for a long nose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A proboscis is a long, bendy nose or snout. Some insects also have one: a long, tube-like mouthpart for sucking up food. «Butterflies drink through a long proboscis that uncurls like a party blower.» Uncurls means unrolls, so the proboscis is something long that can be straightened out.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. «Male proboscis monkeys have long dangling noses that make their calls louder.» The nose hangs down and makes sounds louder, so proboscis must mean a big, dangly nose. Swap the word for nose and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so read the whole sentence. For a butterfly, a proboscis is a drinking tube. For a monkey, it is a nose. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: A proboscis is a long, bendy nose or snout, or a long, tube-like mouthpart on some insects.
fact: «Butterflies» drink nectar, fruit juice and water through a long proboscis.
fact: A butterfly's proboscis stays rolled up, like a party blower, until it is needed.
fact: «Male proboscis monkeys» of Borneo have a long, floppy nose that makes their calls louder.
fact: Proboscis is a grand, funny word for a big nose, but it is also a real word for an insect's drinking tube.
exercise: «Butterflies drink through a long proboscis that uncurls like a party blower.» What is a proboscis in this sentence? | A flower that grows in a garden | *A long, rolled-up drinking tube | A bright coloured wing | A kind of party hat
exercise: «Male proboscis monkeys of Borneo have a long, floppy nose.» What is the proboscis in this sentence? | A kind of wing | *A long, floppy nose | A tree in the jungle | A type of river fish
exercise: «Butterflies cannot chew: they uncurl a long tube called a proboscis to drink.» What does the word called tell you? | The butterfly is hungry and cross | The butterfly is singing | *Proboscis is another name for the long tube | The tube is broken
test: «The proboscis monkey swims well and jumps into rivers from trees.» Is the proboscis here a nose, or a drinking tube? Why? | *A nose, because the sentence is about a monkey | A tree, because monkeys jump from trees | A drinking tube, because monkeys drink nectar | A river, because monkeys swim
test: «Mosquitoes use their proboscis to pierce skin and drink blood.» Which meaning fits, and how do you know? | A wing, because mosquitoes fly | A big, dangly nose, because mosquitoes have noses | A kind of leaf, because mosquitoes live in leaves | *A drinking tube, because it is used to drink
exam: Priya reads, «The butterfly unrolled its proboscis to sip nectar from a flower.» What does proboscis mean here, and what clue shows you? | *A long drinking tube, because the butterfly unrolled it to sip nectar | A big nose, because butterflies have noses | A long drinking tube, because the butterfly sips nectar | A wing, because the butterfly flew away
